  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Analyzing Image Transparency**\n\nI\'ve confirmed that the `IHDR colorType: 6` signifies an RGBA image, meaning transparency is present. The `porto_31e92968.png` file, with dimensions 857x1143, is indeed a transparent cutout PNG! Now, I am exploring how this transparency will interact with layered text.\n\n\n**Exploring Text Layering**\n\nI\'m now focused on how the text layers will interact with the transparent image. I see a compelling example in the reference image `image_66361083.png`, where the text outline visually passes over and under the portrait. The hollow outline effect allows the portrait to be visible through the text stroke, and a solid filled transparent text that layers beneath can be added. I\'m exploring how to replicate this effect with scrolling uppercase geometric sans-serif text like `PORTOFOLIO`.\n\n\n**Refining Marquee Implementation**\n\nI\'m now refining the marquee implementation, focusing on the layers. Layer 1 will be the scrolling \"PORTOFOLIO\" text. Layer 2, Mahesa\'s portrait, and Layer 3 will be a synchronized outline. I\'ll ensure the `-webkit-text-stroke` effects are crisp and consider a monochrome toggle for the portrait. I must also consider the persistent navigation bar.\n\n**Defining Navigation Bar**\n\nI am now clarifying the persistent navigation bar. I need to ensure it remains constant across all pages. The content will be \"Mahesa - About - Experience - Competencies - Certification - Projects - Contact Me\" from left to right.\n\n\n**Clarifying Navigation Details**\n\nI am now focusing on refining the persistent navigation bar details. I need the navigation bar to have a glass effect with a smooth hover animation on each menu item. The content will be \"Mahesa - About - Experience - Competencies - Certification - Projects - Contact Me\" from left to right. I\'m ensuring it remains fixed at the top across all pages, with a centered floating bar styled for a refined glass effect, complete with a monogram icon for \"Mahesa\" that links to the home section, and refined styling for each nav link, with a subtle hover effect.\n\n\n**Defining Menu Interactions**\n\nI\'m now focusing on the interactions for each menu item. They are single-line with smooth hover animations. I\'m prioritizing fluid sliding glass/monochrome highlight pills, subtle underline glides, and smooth text luminance transitions. I also need an active state indicator for the current section. The \"Contact Me\" button on the right will match the \"Hire Me\" button style, with a subtle theme toggle next to it, allowing the user to switch between light and dark monochrome modes.\n\n\n**Prioritizing Image Source**\n\nI\'ve decided we absolutely must *not* invoke `generate_image`. We\'ll exclusively use `/assets/aistudio/porto_31e92968.png` for Mahesa\'s portrait. Instead, I plan to leverage clean monochrome visuals for projects and certifications. I\'m imagining interactive SVG/canvas architectural blueprints, typographic previews, and editorial cards. This guarantees zero broken images and instant loading. I\'m now focused on building pure logic modules and corresponding unit tests, adhering to the decoupling principle from the ultra-mode instructions.\n\n\n**Structuring File Architecture**\n\nI\'m now laying out the core file structure and configurations. I\'m focusing on `/metadata.json` and `/index.html` to set up the application name and description, and I\'m ensuring we load the specified Google Fonts: Outfit, Plus Jakarta Sans, and JetBrains Mono. I\'m preparing a detailed `/src/data/portfolioData.ts` file to hold realistic portfolio data inspired by the user\'s background, including all navigation items.\n\n\n**Defining Content Architecture**\n\nI am now structuring the hero, about, experience, competencies, certifications, and projects content. I\'m focusing on defining the structure for each section, including the hero configuration, the about section content, experience items, competencies categorized into technical, clinical, and leadership, verified certifications, and a curated project portfolio across different categories with interactive previews, with the intent of keeping everything realistic. I\'m also planning `/src/utils/portfolioLogic.ts` pure utility functions.\n\n\n**Implementing Logic Modules**\n\nI\'m now implementing the core utility modules and corresponding unit tests. I\'m building `filterProjects`, `filterCertifications`, `validateContactForm`, and `getMarqueeDuration` in `/src/utils/portfolioLogic.ts`. Comprehensive unit tests are underway in `/src/utils/portfolioLogic.test.ts` using `node:test` and `node:assert/strict` to verify all function logic, with a focus on comprehensive coverage.\n\n\n**Refining Page Sections**\n\nI\'m now focusing on refining the individual page sections, ensuring they each have unique, interactive features. I\'m prioritizing `/components/AboutSection.tsx` with its editorial biography and CV modal. I\'m also working on `/components/ExperienceSection.tsx` with its interactive timeline and `/components/CompetenciesSection.tsx` for its filterable competency matrix. Furthermore, `/components/CertificationSection.tsx` will feature credential showcases, and `/components/ProjectsSection.tsx` will utilize an editorial Bento grid, and `/components/ContactSection.tsx`. All of this uses the `aistudio/porto_31e92968.png` image with crisp typography, a depth outline, and interactive controls to adjust the portrait finish and marquee motion.\n\n\n"
