  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Considering Scroll Behavior**\n\nOkay, I\'m exploring how to implement a smooth scrolling effect on navigation clicks. Native `scrollIntoView` seems like a good starting point, but I\'m trying to decide if it provides the optimal feel. There\'s probably something more responsive.\n\n\n**Refining Animation Implementation**\n\nI\'m now focusing on a custom scrolling engine. I want the scroll effect to be really smooth. The default behavior is okay, but I can improve on that with `requestAnimationFrame`. I\'m going to set it up with a custom easing function, an animation loop of approximately 850ms, and it will scroll to the target section in a cinematic way.\n\n\n"
    tool_calls {
      id: "call_489124"
      name: "replace_file_content"
      arguments_json: "{\"AllowMultiple\":false, \"Description\":\"Add easeInOutQuart and interpolateScrollY pure functions to portfolioLogic.ts\", \"EndLine\":121, \"Instruction\":\"Add smooth scroll easing functions to src/utils/portfolioLogic.ts\", \"ReplacementContent\":\"export function getMarqueeDurationSeconds(speed: \'slow\' | \'normal\' | \'fast\'): number {\\n  switch (speed) {\\n    case \'slow\':\\n      return 38;\\n    case \'fast\':\\n      return 16;\\n    case \'normal\':\\n    default:\\n      return 26;\\n  }\\n}\\n\\n/**\\n * Smooth cinematic easing curve (easeInOutCubic) for programmatic navigation scrolling.\\n */\\nexport function easeInOutCubic(t: number): number {\\n  const clamped = Math.max(0, Math.min(1, t));\\n  return clamped < 0.5\\n    ? 4 * clamped * clamped * clamped\\n    : 1 - Math.pow(-2 * clamped + 2, 3) / 2;\\n}\\n\\nexport function interpolateScrollY(\\n  startY: number,\\n  targetY: number,\\n  progress: number\\n): number {\\n  const eased = easeInOutCubic(progress);\\n  return startY + (targetY - startY) * eased;\\n}\\n\", \"StartLine\":109, \"TargetContent\":\"export function getMarqueeDurationSeconds(speed: \'slow\' | \'normal\' | \'fast\'): number {\\n  switch (speed) {\\n    case \'slow\':\\n      return 38;\\n    case \'fast\':\\n      return 16;\\n    case \'normal\':\\n    default:\\n      return 26;\\n  }\\n}\", \"TargetFile\":\"/src/utils/portfolioLogic.ts\", \"toolAction\":\"Adding smooth scroll easing functions to portfolioLogic.ts\", \"toolSummary\":\"Add scroll easing to portfolioLogic.ts\"}"
