  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Observing Lanyard Details**\n\nI\'ve just focused on the image at `/.playwright-cli/r1-lanyard-about.png`. The 3D Lanyard ID Card in the right column of the `#about` section is fascinating. I\'m noting the printed strap details: \"MAHESA \302\267 PORTOFOLIO \302\267,\" and the metallic clip, ring, and Mahesa\'s portrait.\n\n\n**Critiquing the Framing**\n\nI\'m now deeply analyzing the vertical framing of the 3D Lanyard Card within the image. Specifically, I\'ve noted that the card\'s bottom edge currently touches the canvas due to the `anchorY` and `segmentLength` values. To fix this, I propose adjusting `anchorY` and `segmentLength` in `lanyardPhysics.ts`, or tweaking the camera\'s Y position. This would ensure the card fits perfectly within the viewport, with ample space and mirroring the `fattahmaulana/3D_CARD` example. I\'ve also observed the vertical text orientation on the strap.\n\n\n"
    tool_calls {
      id: "call_367974"
      name: "replace_file_content"
      arguments_json: "{\"AllowMultiple\":false, \"Description\":\"Raise anchorY and calibrate segmentLength in lanyardPhysics.ts so the entire 3D ID card is framed with breathing room at the bottom and strap extending out the top\", \"EndLine\":39, \"Instruction\":\"Update anchorY and seg in createLanyardPhysicsState in src/utils/lanyardPhysics.ts\", \"ReplacementContent\":\"export function createLanyardPhysicsState(): LanyardPhysicsState {\\n  // Start slightly offset to the right (like fattahmaulana/3D_CARD initial swing)\\n  // so the card drops and swings naturally into center on first view.\\n  const anchorY = 4.35;\\n  const seg = 0.68;\\n  const initialOffsets: Vec3[] = [\\n    { x: 0, y: anchorY, z: 0 },\\n    { x: 0.32, y: anchorY - seg * 0.9, z: 0.05 },\\n    { x: 0.65, y: anchorY - seg * 1.8, z: 0.08 },\\n    { x: 0.98, y: anchorY - seg * 2.7, z: 0.1 },\\n    { x: 1.28, y: anchorY - seg * 3.6, z: 0.12 },\\n  ];\", \"StartLine\":22, \"TargetContent\":\"export function createLanyardPhysicsState(): LanyardPhysicsState {\\n  // Start slightly offset to the right (like fattahmaulana/3D_CARD initial swing)\\n  // so the card drops and swings naturally into center on first view.\\n  const anchorY = 3.6;\\n  const seg = 0.85;\\n  const initialOffsets: Vec3[] = [\\n    { x: 0, y: anchorY, z: 0 },\\n    { x: 0.35, y: anchorY - seg * 0.9, z: 0.05 },\\n    { x: 0.72, y: anchorY - seg * 1.8, z: 0.08 },\\n    { x: 1.08, y: anchorY - seg * 2.7, z: 0.1 },\\n    { x: 1.42, y: anchorY - seg * 3.6, z: 0.12 },\\n  ];\", \"TargetFile\":\"/src/utils/lanyardPhysics.ts\", \"toolAction\":\"Updating anchorY and rope segment length in lanyardPhysics.ts\", \"toolSummary\":\"Update anchor and segment length in lanyardPhysics.ts\"}"
