  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Analyzing Lanyard Details**\n\nI\'ve started meticulously examining the lanyard in the provided video segments. My focus is on every detail of its appearance and how it moves. I\'m paying close attention to the specific timestamps you requested, 00:01 to 00:08 and 00:54 to 01:00, seeking to thoroughly understand its properties.\n\n\n**Observing Visual Placement**\n\nI\'ve just made a significant discovery: the 3D lanyard isn\'t enclosed in a box as I initially expected. Examining the video from timestamps 00:02-00:06 and 00:55-01:00, I see it\'s set against a transparent background and positioned directly within the \"About\" section, with its strap hanging from the top. Moreover, the lanyard appears to drop down from the top as the user enters the \"About\" section (00:01-00:02).\n\n\n**Confirming Dynamic Behavior**\n\nI\'m now integrating the understanding of the lanyard\'s dynamic behavior upon entering the \"About\" section. Specifically, at timestamp 00:03, I\'m verifying the card\'s behavior: it should start high, above the top, and fall under gravity with realistic bouncing. The goal is a visual drop into place on the right side of the \"About\" section as a smooth visual transition. To that end, I\'ll use `IntersectionObserver` to trigger `resetAndDropLanyard` to make sure it functions as it should, for every transition into `#about` with threshold of `0.15`.\nI\'m also removing any interactive buttons or unnecessary elements like headers, bottom bars, or dark card backgrounds.\n\n\n**Defining Visual Elements**\n\nI\'m now zeroing in on the finer visual details of the lanyard and ID card, particularly from timestamps 00:03-00:08. The lanyard strap is a sleek black, showcasing clean white text. The ID card features a black metallic clip, and a vertical portrait style. It has \"PORTOFOLIO / 2026\" and \"MAHESA / POLTEKKES\" badges. The card features a portrait of Mahesa, with a dark gradient vignette at the bottom. Finally, a white signature and job description sits over the gradient. I\'m focusing on making the model interactive via grabbing.\n\n\n**Eliminating Location Detail**\n\nI\'m removing the location indicator, \"Semarang, Jawa Tengah, Indonesia,\" from the `#about` section. I\'ve pinpointed the relevant CSS selectors and will remove the corresponding code block in `AboutSection.tsx`. This frees space at the top-right of the \"About\" section, allowing the lanyard\'s strap to visually attach to the very top, directly above the heading and description.\n\n\n"
    tool_calls {
      id: "call_2247"
      name: "write_to_file"
      arguments_json: "{\"CodeContent\":\"export interface Vec3 {\\n  x: number;\\n  y: number;\\n  z: number;\\n}\\n\\nexport interface LanyardNode {\\n  pos: Vec3;\\n  prevPos: Vec3;\\n  lerped: Vec3;\\n  pinned: boolean;\\n}\\n\\nexport interface LanyardPhysicsState {\\n  nodes: LanyardNode[]; // [0]=fixed anchor at top edge, [1]=j1, [2]=j2, [3]=j3, [4]=card\\n  segmentLength: number;\\n  rot: Vec3;\\n  angVel: Vec3;\\n  isDragged: boolean;\\n  dragTarget: Vec3;\\n}\\n\\nexport function createLanyardPhysicsState(): LanyardPhysicsState {\\n  // Anchor [0] is pinned at the very top edge of the About section viewport (y = 4.65).\\n  // Free nodes [1..4] start high above the top edge so the lanyard drops down from above\\n  // when entering the About section.\\n  const anchorY = 4.65;\\n  const seg = 0.72;\\n\\n  const state: LanyardPhysicsState = {\\n    nodes: [\\n      {\\n        pos: { x: 0, y: anchorY, z: 0 },\\n        prevPos: { x: 0, y: anchorY, z: 0 },\\n        lerped: { x: 0, y: anchorY, z: 0 },\\n        pinned: true,\\n      },\\n      {\\n        pos: { x: 0.18, y: anchorY + 0.6, z: 0.04 },\\n        prevPos: { x: 0.12, y: anchorY + 0.75, z: 0.04 },\\n        lerped: { x: 0.18, y: anchorY + 0.6, z: 0.04 },\\n        pinned: false,\\n      },\\n      {\\n        pos: { x: 0.36, y: anchorY + 1.1, z: 0.08 },\\n        prevPos: { x: 0.25, y: anchorY + 1.3, z: 0.08 },\\n        lerped: { x: 0.36, y: anchorY + 1.1, z: 0.08 },\\n        pinned: false,\\n      },\\n      {\\n        pos: { x: 0.54, y: anchorY + 1.5, z: 0.12 },\\n        prevPos: { x: 0.38, y: anchorY + 1.75, z: 0.12 },\\n        lerped: { x: 0.54, y: anchorY + 1.5, z: 0.12 },\\n        pinned: false,\\n      },\\n      {\\n        pos: { x: 0.72, y: anchorY + 1.9, z: 0.16 },\\n        prevPos: { x: 0.52, y: anchorY + 2.2, z: 0.16 },\\n        lerped: { x: 0.72, y: anchorY + 1.9, z: 0.16 },\\n        pinned: false,\\n      },\\n    ],\\n    segmentLength: seg,\\n    rot: { x: -0.12, y: 0.35, z: 0.18 },\\n    angVel: { x: 0, y: -1.8, z: 0 },\\n    isDragged: false,\\n    dragTarget: { x: 0, y: 0, z: 0 },\\n  };\\n\\n  return state;\\n}\\n\\nexport function resetLanyardDrop(state: LanyardPhysicsState): void {\\n  const fresh = createLanyardPhysicsState();\\n  state.nodes = fresh.nodes;\\n  state.rot = fresh.rot;\\n  state.angVel = fresh.angVel;\\n  state.isDragged = false;\\n}\\n\\nexport function stepLanyardPhysics(\\n  state: LanyardPhysicsState,\\n  dt: number\\n): void {\\n  const safeDt = Math.min(Math.max(dt, 0.001), 0.033);\\n  const gravityY = -38.0;\\n  const damping = Math.pow(0.22, safeDt);\\n\\n  // 1. Verlet integration for free nodes\\n  for (let i = 1; i < state.nodes.length; i++) {\\n    const node = state.nodes[i];\\n    if (i === 4 && state.isDragged) {\\n      node.prevPos.x = node.pos.x;\\n      node.prevPos.y = node.pos.y;\\n      node.prevPos.z = node.pos.z;\\n      node.pos.x += (state.dragTarget.x - node.pos.x) * 0.45;\\n      node.pos.y += (state.dragTarget.y - node.pos.y) * 0.45;\\n      node.pos.z += (state.dragTarget.z - node.pos.z) * 0.45;\\n      continue;\\n    }\\n\\n    const vx = (node.pos.x - node.prevPos.x) * damping;\\n    const vy = (node.pos.y - node.prevPos.y) * damping;\\n    const vz = (node.pos.z - node.prevPos.z) * damping;\\n\\n    node.prevPos.x = node.pos.x;\\n    node.prevPos.y = node.pos.y;\\n    node.prevPos.z = node.pos.z;\\n\\n    node.pos.x += vx;\\n    node.pos.y += vy + gravityY * safeDt * safeDt;\\n    node.pos.z += vz;\\n  }\\n\\n  // 2. Solve rope distance constraints iteratively\\n  const iterations = 12;\\n  for (let iter = 0; iter < iterations; iter++) {\\n    for (let i = 0; i < state.nodes.length - 1; i++) {\\n      const a = state.nodes[i];\\n      const b = state.nodes[i + 1];\\n\\n      const dx = b.pos.x - a.pos.x;\\n      const dy = b.pos.y - a.pos.y;\\n      const dz = b.pos.z - a.pos.z;\\n      const dist = Math.hypot(dx, dy, dz) || 0.0001;\\n      const diff = (dist - state.segmentLength) / dist;\\n\\n      const aLocked = a.pinned;\\n      const bLocked = i + 1 === 4 && state.isDragged;\\n\\n      if (aLocked && !bLocked) {\\n        b.pos.x -= dx * diff;\\n        b.pos.y -= dy * diff;\\n        b.pos.z -= dz * diff;\\n      } else if (!aLocked && bLocked) {\\n        a.pos.x += dx * diff;\\n        a.pos.y += dy * diff;\\n        a.pos.z += dz * diff;\\n      } else if (!aLocked && !bLocked) {\\n        const weightA = i + 1 === 4 ? 0.72 : 0.5;\\n        const weightB = 1 - weightA;\\n        a.pos.x += dx * diff * weightA;\\n        a.pos.y += dy * diff * weightA;\\n        a.pos.z += dz * diff * weightA;\\n        b.pos.x -= dx * diff * weightB;\\n        b.pos.y -= dy * diff * weightB;\\n        b.pos.z -= dz * diff * weightB;\\n      }\\n    }\\n  }\\n\\n  // 3. Smooth lerped positions for intermediate joints\\n  const minSpeed = 12;\\n  const maxSpeed = 55;\\n  for (let i = 1; i <= 2; i++) {\\n    const node = state.nodes[i];\\n    const dist = Math.hypot(\\n      node.pos.x - node.lerped.x,\\n      node.pos.y - node.lerped.y,\\n      node.pos.z - node.lerped.z\\n    );\\n    const clampedDist = Math.max(0.1, Math.min(1.0, dist));\\n    const factor = Math.min(\\n      1,\\n      safeDt * (minSpeed + clampedDist * (maxSpeed - minSpeed))\\n    );\\n    node.lerped.x += (node.pos.x - node.lerped.x) * factor;\\n    node.lerped.y += (node.pos.y - node.lerped.y) * factor;\\n    node.lerped.z += (node.pos.z - node.lerped.z) * factor;\\n  }\\n  state.nodes[0].lerped = { ...state.nodes[0].pos };\\n  state.nodes[3].lerped = { ...state.nodes[3].pos };\\n  state.nodes[4].lerped = { ...state.nodes[4].pos };\\n\\n  // 4. Card rotational kinematics & spring return\\n  const j3 = state.nodes[3].pos;\\n  const card = state.nodes[4].pos;\\n  const cardVx = (card.x - state.nodes[4].prevPos.x) / safeDt;\\n  const cardVz = (card.z - state.nodes[4].prevPos.z) / safeDt;\\n\\n  const targetRotZ = Math.max(\\n    -0.55,\\n    Math.min(0.55, (card.x - j3.x) * 0.65)\\n  );\\n  const targetRotX = Math.max(\\n    -0.35,\\n    Math.min(0.35, -(card.z - j3.z) * 0.65 + cardVz * 0.015)\\n  );\\n\\n  state.rot.z += (targetRotZ - state.rot.z) * Math.min(1, safeDt * 12);\\n  state.rot.x += (targetRotX - state.rot.x) * Math.min(1, safeDt * 12);\\n\\n  state.angVel.y += (-state.rot.y * 10.5 + cardVx * 0.45) * safeDt;\\n  state.angVel.y *= Math.pow(0.12, safeDt);\\n  state.rot.y += state.angVel.y * safeDt;\\n}\\n\", \"Description\":\"Update lanyardPhysics.ts so the lanyard starts above the top edge and drops from above when entering the About section\", \"Overwrite\":true, \"TargetFile\":\"/src/utils/lanyardPhysics.ts\", \"toolAction\":\"Updating lanyardPhysics.ts for top-down drop animation\", \"toolSummary\":\"Update lanyardPhysics.ts for drop animation\"}"
      thinking_signature: "\022\334/\n\331/\001i\024}\023x\246\343k\305\304\304JC_r\n\340a\333ND\211\363\315\227\210w\210\v\001+e\327\354\366\301\310\372\325\325\022\346f>\216\304k,\241\377\3377\306s\202\207`P(w\304)i6\024L\000!\266\257\322K\246\303u\356-\037_5\004\311_\260TN\217\000\347j\254y*v\005\377.\034\343\336\330\314\202\004\b>\235xc\371\270\340}o\362\251\250\324\326p\205\023=x\361utX\205\366\245\341\276\a\b\253z\263h^2\257\027`\333\227$\b\233M\030\364\233\tVj9\243\316\377\266t|`Xs<\371\n!\\{\377\016\265=\344m\325M8\2705WB\206Z#\037_\323d \037\311>\004\344\221\273\363\357\353\213\302w\274\265\353\3607F\2530\3739I\225S\345#\252\306\214\347O\0251\005L\231\\\244\001\355\232\241\235\310\264Kr\022\362/\310fm\237\333\202\272\227e\313\274g\230g\341.\257D\022\351\210\312\376!93X\353\211u\\(\347?g\216\025\035\337\a\"B\366#&{\354\231\n\266\r,\b\215\262m}_LT\273`\020\237\n\351F\323\271\200`\' \206\000\324\245\034\253x.F\033\375\223v\272\364\256\223G\310:\264l\277\361\374\001\\\303(\356Z\350n\"<4\216:%\204*\217\357ykm4\323\266\355\226x\372\306:\036u4\350$\\\2137\276ZS\031\2441!Sf\245 \b\323\370\251q_\301\234\251+\200\341Q\230Z8\3520Vx\240\212\257\322\226b]\235\340\017\250\310\230u\340\036]\031\240\000\301>\316y\273\324\334\037\346\260\323\352Z`\213b\232\233G\277(\367\030\301\371\321\027\370k\t\355_\v\n\341\204\237\206\375\027/\177\220\312\f_\321\272\'\256-\256\315\3043\r\331\305\235N\310\037,\245\333\333\311ps\037\034,\300\246\351A\305\'>u\223\0179\241B\210\324\202\216t$\336\227\321\203\021Y\270\257\032\307D)-*c\204O:y\350W#\233B\203\271)\bV\352\263\251e+\366\274_,\345P\025\f\257\234`@\217FX\254\364\371\271\246`!\271ST\372\b\031\025\334y\200\274\336-\352\215\272\346\210\206M\300|\325\224*@FQ\275N\312fDS\340|\005\262\273\205\365\254Ae.g\001\262\300\023\246Yo\\c\317\357\b6\\* \222\f-Q\330#u\255\252\343\024\365G\270\316}\242\267\2507\257xl\350UtT\021\365\023\344\365\240=j\n\203\305\004\274\244U\203\353\361\216O\242\265V\322TP\371\345)nA[\321gh\317M\035\246\234\300^|\250y\02