  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Analyzing Lanyard Clipping**\n\nI see it now! Examining the image at `/public/assets/aistudio/image_d0132e03.png` completely clarifies why the lanyard wasn\'t being clipped properly. This image shows the issue perfectly.\n\n\n**Expanding Lanyard Canvas**\n\nI\'ve realized the `<Lanyard3DCard />` was confined to a column. I want the WebGL canvas to occupy the entire `#about` section, but I\'m considering potential conflicts with button clicks on the left. The plan is to set `pointer-events-none` on the full-section canvas wrapper. I\'ll need to figure out how to attach `pointermove` and `pointerdown` events to it.\n\n\n**Implementing Pointer Interactions**\n\nI\'m now focusing on pointer events. My current goal is a system where the 3D lanyard responds to the user\'s interaction across the entire section. When the pointer is over the lanyard, it\'ll capture events and allow for free dragging. Otherwise, clicks will function on the buttons and text as expected. I\'m leaning toward dynamically toggling `renderer.domElement.style.pointerEvents`, or listening to `pointerdown`, `pointermove`, and `pointerup` on the wrapper, given `pointer-events-none`.\n\n\n**Tracing Pointer Events**\n\nI\'ve been tracing the `pointerdown` and `pointermove` events. I see that even with `pointer-events-none` on the full-bleed canvas overlay, the events are still firing! The buttons and text selection under the overlay still work as expected. The goal is now to enable dragging the 3D card only when a user interacts with it. When `onPointerMove` detects an interaction with the 3D card, I will set `domEl.style.pointerEvents = \'auto\'`.\n\n\n**Refining Pointer Logic**\n\nI\'ve refined the pointer logic. Now, as the mouse moves onto the 3D card, raycasting with the meshes (`frameMesh`, `frontMesh`, `backMesh`) determines interaction. A `hits.length > 0` condition triggers `domEl.style.pointerEvents = \'auto\'` and `cursor: \'grab\'`. When the user drags, the card can move freely across the whole width of the page. Once the mouse leaves the card, `hits.length === 0` sets `domEl.style.pointerEvents = \'none\'` again, letting the buttons beneath be clickable.\n\n\n**Verifying 3D Position**\n\nI\'m now verifying the 3D position of the lanyard anchor when the canvas spans the full width of the section. With calculations for a `1440x820` viewport, the horizontal frustum at `z=0` ranges from `-5.47` to `+5.47` and the right column is centered around `x \342\211\210 +1.95`. This needs to be confirmed.\n\n\n**Confirming Canvas Dragging**\n\nI\'ve just confirmed the drag behavior on a 1440px viewport.  With x = 1.95 centered in the right column, the 3D card can be dragged across the entire width of the screen: 7.4 units to the left and 3.5 units to the right! The lanyard\'s canvas is completely unconstrained by a box! The y coordinates will go from +0.95 down to -3.11. This verifies full-bleed dragging!\n\n\n**Updating Lanyard Text**\n\nI\'m now changing the text on the front of the 3D lanyard card. I\'ve updated the script to render \"Perekam Medis dan Informasi Kesehatan\" in place of \"MAHESA RIZKY PUTRA I.\" I\'ll need to remove the text underneath that, and I will be done.\n\n\n\n**Adjusting Lanyard Text**\n\nI\'ve deleted the text beneath \"Perekam Medis dan Informasi Kesehatan\" and adjusted the canvas accordingly. I\'ve also updated `createCardBackTexture` to ensure consistency when the card flips. I confirmed the font size fits with ample margins, so the position of the signature, accent line, and text are set!\n\n\n**Validating Lanyard Physics**\n\nI\'ve been validating the physics with different anchor configurations. I\'ve confirmed that changing `anchorX` to `1.95` or `0` works flawlessly. I\'ve also revisited `onPointerMove` and confirmed the dragTarget.x coordinates, and clarified they now range from -4.5 to +4.5.\n\n\n**Clarifying Full-Width Rendering**\n\nI now understand the previous limitations! The card was boxed in because `<div className=\"lg:col-span-5\">` confined the `<canvas>`, and `dragTarget.x` was clamped. I can now drag the lanyard freely with the `canvas` occupying the entire section and `dragTarget.x` ranging from -4.5 to +4.5.\n\n\n**Calculating Lanyard Anchor**\n\nI\'m now calculating `anchorX`, so the 3D lanyard always aligns with the right column on desktop, and is centered on mobile. The canvas\'s visible height is about `6.232` world units. With the camera set at a distance of `12.5`, I\'ll use this ratio to calculate anchor positions.\n\n\n**Refining Anchor Calculation**\n\nMy calculation refines the lanyard\'s positioning logic.  I\'ve converted pixel offsets to 3D world units, confirming the anchor\'s x-coordinate is +2.556, which positions the lanyard correctly within the right column. I need to test this on smaller widths.\n\n\n"
    tool_calls {
      id: "call_268242"
      name: "replace_file_content"
      arguments_json: "{\"AllowMultiple\":false, \"Description\":\"Support configurable anchorX in createLanyardPhysicsState and resetLanyardDrop so the lanyard can anchor on the right side of a full-width unclipped canvas\", \"EndLine\":80, \"Instruction\":\"Update createLanyardPhysicsState and resetLanyardDrop in /src/utils/lanyardPhysics.ts to accept anchorX\", \"ReplacementContent\":\"export interface LanyardPhysicsState {\\n  nodes: LanyardNode[]; // [0]=fixed anchor at top edge, [1]=j1, [2]=j2, [3]=j3, [4]=card\\n  anchorX: number;\\n  segmentLength: number;\\n  rot: Vec3;\\n  angVel: Vec3;\\n  isDragged: boolean;\\n  dragTarget: Vec3;\\n}\\n\\nexport function createLanyardPhysicsState(anchorX = 0): LanyardPhysicsState {\\n  // Anchor [0] is pinned at the top edge of the About section frustum (y = 3.15).\\n  // Free nodes [1..4] start above the top edge so the lanyard drops down from above\\n  // when entering the About section and settles in the right-hand space.\\n  const anchorY = 3.15;\\n  const seg = 0.55;\\n\\n  const state: LanyardPhysicsState = {\\n    nodes: [\\n      {\\n        pos: { x: anchorX, y: anchorY, z: 0 },\\n        prevPos: { x: anchorX, y: anchorY, z: 0 },\\n        lerped: { x: anchorX, y: anchorY, z: 0 },\\n        pinned: true,\\n      },\\n      {\\n        pos: { x: anchorX + 0.12, y: anchorY + 0.45, z: 0.03 },\\n        prevPos: { x: anchorX + 0.08, y: anchorY + 0.55, z: 0.03 },\\n        lerped: { x: anchorX + 0.12, y: anchorY + 0.45, z: 0.03 },\\n        pinned: false,\\n      },\\n      {\\n        pos: { x: anchorX + 0.24, y: anchorY + 0.85, z: 0.06 },\\n        prevPos: { x: anchorX + 0.18, y: anchorY + 1.0, z: 0.06 },\\n        lerped: { x: anchorX + 0.24, y: anchorY + 0.85, z: 0.06 },\\n        pinned: false,\\n      },\\n      {\\n        pos: { x: anchorX + 0.35, y: anchorY + 1.25, z: 0.09 },\\n        prevPos: { x: anchorX + 0.26, y: anchorY + 1.45, z: 0.09 },\\n        lerped: { x: anchorX + 0.35, y: anchorY + 1.25, z: 0.09 },\\n        pinned: false,\\n      },\\n      {\\n        pos: { x: anchorX + 0.46, y: anchorY + 1.65, z: 0.12 },\\n        prevPos: { x: anchorX + 0.34, y: anchorY + 1.9, z: 0.12 },\\n        lerped: { x: anchorX + 0.46, y: anchorY + 1.65, z: 0.12 },\\n        pinned: false,\\n      },\\n    ],\\n    anchorX,\\n    segmentLength: seg,\\n    rot: { x: -0.08, y: 0.28, z: 0.14 },\\n    angVel: { x: 0, y: -1.4, z: 0 },\\n    isDragged: false,\\n    dragTarget: { x: anchorX, y: 0, z: 0 },\\n  };\\n\\n  return state;\\n}\\n\\nexport function setLanyardAnchorX(\\n  state: LanyardPhysicsState,\\n  newAnchorX: number\\n): void {\\n  const dx = newAnchorX - state.anchorX;\\n  state.anchorX = newAnchorX;\\n  for (const node of state.nodes) {\\n    node.pos.x += dx;\\n    node.prevPos.x += dx;\\n    node.lerped.x += dx;\\n  }\\n}\\n\\nexport function resetLanyardDrop(state: LanyardPhysicsState): void {\\n  const fresh = createLanyardPhysicsState(state.anchorX);\\n  state.nodes = fresh.nodes;\\n  state.rot = fresh.rot;\\n  state.angVel = fresh.angVel;\\n  state.isDragged = false;\\n}\", \"StartLine\":14, \"TargetContent\":\"export interface LanyardPhysicsState {\\n  nodes: LanyardNode[]; // [0]=fixed anchor at top edge, [1]=j1, [2]=j2, [3]=j3, [4]=card\\n  segmentLength: number;\\n  rot: Vec3;\\n  angVel: Vec3;\\n  isDragged: boolean;\\n  dragTarget: Vec3;\\n}\\n\\nexport function createLanyardPhysicsState(): LanyardPhysicsState {\\n  // Anchor [0] is pinned at the top edge of the About section frustum (y = 3.15).\\n  // Free nodes [1..4] start above the top edge so the lanyard drops down from above\\n  // when entering the About section and settles in the right-hand space.\\n  const anchorY = 3.15;\\n  const seg = 0.55;\\n\\n  const state: LanyardPhysicsState = {\\n    nodes: [\\n      {\\n        pos: { x: 0, y: anchorY, z: 0 },\\n        prevPos: { x: 0, y: anchorY, z: 0 },\\n        lerped: { x: 0, y: anchorY, z: 0 },\\n        pinned: true,\\n      },\\n      {\\n        pos: { x: 0.12, y: anchorY + 0.45, z: 0.03 },\\n        prevPos: { x: 0.08, y: anchorY + 0.55, z: 0.03 },\\n        lerped: { x: 0.12, y: anchorY + 0.45, z: 0.03 },\\n        pinned: false,\\n      },\\n      {\\n        pos: { x: 0.24, y: anchorY + 0.85, z: 0.06 },\\n        prevPos: { x: 0.18, y: anchorY + 1.0, z: 0.06 },\\n        lerped: { x: 0.24, y: anchorY + 0.85, z: 0.06 },\\n        pinned: false,\\n      },\\n      {\\n        pos: { x: 0.35, y: anchorY + 1.25, z: 0.09 },\\n        prevPos: { x: 0.26, y: anchorY + 1.45, z: 0.09 },\\n        lerped: { x: 0.35, y: anchorY + 1.25, z: 0.09 },\\n        pinned: false,\\n      },\\n      {\\n        pos: { x: 0.46, y: anchorY + 1.65, z: 0.12 },\\n        prevPos: { x: 0.34, y: anchorY + 1.9, z: 0.12 },\\n        lerped: { x: 0.46, y: anchorY + 1.65, z: 0.12 },\\n        pinned: false,\\n      },\\n    ],\\n    segmentLength: seg,\\n    rot: { x: -0.08, y: 0.28, z: 0.14 },\\n    angVel: { x: 0, y: -1.4, z: 0 },\\n    isDragged: false,\\n    dragTarget: { x: 0, y: 0, z: 0 },\\n  };\\n\\n  return state;\\n}\\n\\nexport function resetLanyardDrop(state: LanyardPhysicsState): void {\\n  const fresh = createLanyardPhysicsState();\\n  state.nodes = fresh.nodes;\\n  state.rot = fresh.rot;\\n  state.angVel = fresh.angVel;\\n  state.isDragged = false;\\n}\", \"TargetFile\":\"/src/utils/lanyardPhysics.ts\", \"toolAction\":\"Adding anchorX support to lanyardPhysics.ts\", \"toolSummary\":\"Add anchorX support to lanyardPhysics.ts\"}"
      thinking_signature: "\022\205}\n\202}\001i\024}\023\344S~\376o\272\224\260K\337\025P\356\345\247\367\374\330\001v\346^D\320\247\026v\350\021\r7I\244\317\270\000\035Km@\a\243\021\217\177\325\227\r\265\222\327\342\320\373\257`f&\236z\214}\341\037=`\223h\342\2210\0233\016\026\242\351c\026\321\000xl\320\033\023\200\241\335\244\367u\030n\3760g\333\326\264:\027\022\222\020\200\360h!l\263\335\r\330\253\254\266d\341\003D\252\312\327>K\247Y\250\211\2760\036\201\205yH\352f\273\223\034\206\322\215\245\250\366\354\360\026\221\231\346&\367\264)\000\326\334\216\363\237d\236M\263\206\220\300\235\323n\263^;\261\325\265\332\324\331KUUe\364by\245\257\250\251\314\210\327\345%`LZ\\\251\017k\032\032\002\325\251AT\002\\\200:\\\016\016M\255\006\311\231\356\341\336\301\330\233\237\365\351\235JN\246,\236\317\006mG\264\232\340\340\277\332J|\205B^FL\005\250YkQ?E\347\232\306\2512\276!T\022b0\231\275K\377\225\024P\330e\307WBm[!0aK>\024\314\034l\316\310\342\374\n&\373_\026\370\353\223\364\220\303\210\245\037R\220V\352\230\035 \3553\316\217GZ\337\232c)\263\333\272\267\2376\002\313O\224\3000\"e\212\301\220\255\272\356\212\211\201\310g\031\360s[o\016\275\0272*\025\307y\000J\3131Y%\274!1+\210\244\002\2573\231\326\205q\274\002\025\235 [\252y\325MZx4\244T \022\246Fc\206\030\254C0m\177\263\231\215\203\200\355\272kJ\323\363$\257k5B\226A\255\026\024\252\202>\272\206\226\333\352\260l\314\377w\254{\341\210\n\236\200\331\254_\037\347\206gVT\323\by\377\337\033h\177\260\262\213ydm\v\211\230I?\036/V\2516\000\343\346\320\347\3267#\234\216&\331%\0250\351\302\230B\377\263{\322\030\374\233\344\364\023\355\254\340\240\343\022X\315\2679\352\234F\002f(,w\251h\347\224\207\231\023|7pNDE\230\205M]\324\002\266\207\354qY\362\023\327[\002\221\203\256\337\232\234\t\354\020\r11\026?\026\343\206\204j%,\035\314\374\367~J\205.\232g:\240\262\213\254\210\234p\302\315\327\354\2555@>\276@\334\341\330\366*\361\377}\366\2777tjH\002}\234id\337\260[\371\362\'\016\207f\006\262\214&\032E\213\335\353x\345$:\002\346\374c\034,\241\235