  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Observing File Downloads**\n\nI\'ve just observed Playwright downloading a PDF, specifically `CV_ATS_7ce604eb.pdf`, as indicated in the console log. The file is being saved in the `.playwright-cli` directory. This seems like a critical piece of the puzzle!\n\n\n**Analyzing PDF Rendering**\n\nI\'m now focused on why the iframe download occurred with the PDF. It seems sandboxed iframes or browsers without PDF plugins cause this, leading to the download instead of displaying the document. My goal is to create a reliable, interactive PDF viewer for `/assets/aistudio/CV_ATS_7ce604eb.pdf`, working in all browsers. I\'m exploring solutions like `pdfjs-dist` or pre-rendering to `<canvas>` images to avoid the download. The plan includes zoom and navigation controls, with an \"Unduh PDF\" button. I\'m also considering checks to determine whether `pdftoppm` or `pdfjs-dist` is already available for simplicity.\n\n\n"
    tool_calls {
      id: "call_433215"
